      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "With the aid of infrared thermography, a powerful new tool for studying the biological state of cardiac regulatory mechanisms, the reversal of the isoproterenol-induced calorigenic action in the in situ dog heart was demonstrated after establishing acute myocardial ischemia. The thermographic manifestations indicated a modified activity pattern of the cardiac (coronary) beta-mechanism with a preserved sensitivity to its specific pharmacologic blockade. Results provide new evidence of the transformation (plasticity) of adrenoceptor qualities under pathologic circumstances."},
